  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Noor Mohammad vs State on 3 October, 2017 Author: Sabina Bench: Sabina In The High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Cr. Revision Petition No. 481/2001. Noor Mohammad S/o Shri Abdul Gaffar, by caste Musalman, R/o Kathun, Distt. Kota (Rajasthan).",
    "facts": "Appeal filed by the petitioner was dismissed by the Appellate Court vide order dated 30.6.2001.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that the independent witness had not supported the prosecution case. Be that as it may, learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner under Section 7/16 of the Act. Learned Counsel has submitted that the sentence qua imprisonment of the petitioner be reduced to the period already undergone by him as the petitioner is facing the criminal proceedings since the year 1989. Petitioner is now suffering from various old age ailments. Learned counsel has placed reliance on the decision of Punjab & Haryana High Court in Puran Mal Vs. State of Haryana 2009(4) R.C.R. (Criminal) 527.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that the independent witness had not supported the prosecution case. Be that as it may, learned counsel has submitted that he does not challenge the conviction of the petitioner under Section 7/16 of the Act. Learned Counsel has submitted that the sentence qua imprisonment of the petitioner be reduced to the period already undergone by him as the petitioner is facing the criminal proceedings since the year 1989. Petitioner is now suffering from various old age ailments. Learned counsel has placed reliance on the decision of Punjab & Haryana High Court in Puran Mal Vs. State of Haryana 2009(4) R.C.R. (Criminal) 527.",
